<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Prompts</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>System Rule</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A single, fixed system rule was used for all experiments to prime the models for the task. This rule defines the persona of the AI assistant and the expected numerical format for answers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
        
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System Rule</span></p>
</div>
        
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
You are a helpful AI assistant in a world where mathematical notation has changed. Use only the provided context. Always answer using decimal numbers only.
</span></p>
</div>
      
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Instruction Variants</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Four distinct instruction variants were tested to assess the impact of output formatting requirements on model performance. Each prompt included exactly one of these variants appended to the System Rule.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
        
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Instruction Variant 1</span></p>
</div>
        
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
Instruction:\nPresent your solution in the following format:\n1. Interpret the transformation rules.\n2. Apply them step by step.\n3. Justify each transformation.\n4. Final Answer: LaTeX \boxed{answer}.
</span></p>
</div>
      
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
        
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Instruction Variant 2</span></p>
</div>
        
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
Instruction:\nSolve the problem by:\n1. Explaining the transformation logic.\n2. Showing the intermediate steps clearly.\n3. Justifying each step briefly.\n4. Final Answer: LaTeX \boxed{answer}.
</span></p>
</div>
      
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.4" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
        
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Instruction Variant 3</span></p>
</div>
        
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
Instruction:\nSolve the problem and present only the final result as LaTeX \boxed{answer}.
</span></p>
</div>
      
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.5" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
        
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Instruction Variant 4</span></p>
</div>
        
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
Instruction:\nCompute the correct result. Provide the answer only. Output: \boxed{answer}\n
</span></p>
</div>
      
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Experimental Approaches</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two primary experimental approaches were designed to evaluate different modes of reasoning.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.1 </span>Descriptive Approach (Hint-Based)</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this approach, the prompt explicitly provides the model with a natural language hint describing the mathematical transformations. This tests the model’s ability to interpret and apply predefined rules.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generated Hint Examples</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The hint text is generated by the <span id="A1.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">transforms_to_prompt</span> function based on the specific transformation applied. Below are examples of hints for each transformation type.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="A1.I1" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="A1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Swap Symbols</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">The operator mapping was applied, where operator ’+’ is transformed into ’*’ and operator ’/’ is transformed into ’-’.</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Swap Digits</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">The digits 2 and 8 were exchanged.</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reverse Place Values</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">The place values of digits were reversed (e.g., 123 <math id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 321).</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rotate Digits</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Each number had its digits rotated right by 2 position(s), excluding decimal parts.</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Add Constant</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A constant value of 5 was added to the expression.</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Negate Result</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">The entire expression was negated.</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix7" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modular Arithmetic</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Modulo arithmetic was applied with modulo 7.</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix8" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Trig Substitution</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Trigonometric substitution was applied: replaced 45 with math.cos(90°).</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix9" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Change Base</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">The numeral system was changed to base 8.</span></p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, a concluding note is often appended, such as: <span id="A1.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Note: Digit transformations modify the representation of numbers, including the final computed result.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.2 </span>Inductive Approach (Example-Based)</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this approach, the prompt contains no hint. The model must infer the hidden mathematical rules solely from the provided few-shot examples (or from the problem statement in the zero-shot case). This tests the model’s ability to recognize patterns and generalize from data.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Complete Prompt Examples</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following examples illustrate the raw prompt structure for different experimental configurations, using a hypothetical transformation where the digits ‘1‘ and ‘7‘ are swapped.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.4.1 </span>Inductive, 2-Shot, Instruction Variant 1</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model must infer the “swap 1 and 7” rule from the two examples and provide a step-by-step solution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
          
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System Message</span></p>
</div>
          
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
You are a helpful AI assistant in a world where mathematical notation has changed. Use only the provided context. Always answer using decimal numbers only.\n\nInstruction:\nPresent your solution in the following format:\n1. Interpret the transformation rules.\n2. Apply them step by step.\n3. Justify each transformation.\n4. Final Answer: LaTeX \boxed{answer}.
</span></p>
</div>
        
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
          
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User Message</span></p>
</div>
          
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
Examples:\n1. 10 * 3 = \boxed{210}\n2. 81 - 1 = \boxed{80}\n\nProblem:\n11 + 77 = \boxed{?}
</span></p>
</div>
        
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.4.2 </span>Descriptive, 0-Shot, Instruction Variant 4</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model is explicitly told the rule via a hint and must provide only the final answer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
          
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System Message</span></p>
</div>
          
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
You are a helpful AI assistant in a world where mathematical notation has changed. Use only the provided context. Always answer using decimal numbers only.\n\nInstruction:\nCompute the correct result. Provide the answer only. Output: \boxed{answer}\n
</span></p>
</div>
        
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
          
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User Message</span></p>
</div>
          
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
Problem:\n(Hint: The digits 1 and 7 were exchanged.)\n11 + 77 = \boxed{?}
</span></p>
</div>
        
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Hyperparameters</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following table details the hyperparameters used for all fine-tuning experiments. The hyperparameters were selected through manual tuning. We chose the final values based on the best performance observed on a validation set.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Key hyperparameters for QLoRA fine-tuning.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A2.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
